parameters.description:
The filter should like: [{"id":"domain_status", "logic":{}, "value":["allowed"]}], then URL encode this filter string and put this in filter parameter.

The available "id" of filter are ["domain_status", "resource_type"].

Example: { "id": "domain_status", "logic": { "is": { "string": true } }, "value": ["allowed"] }

Example: { "id": "resource_type", "logic": { "is": { "string": true } }, "value": ["script", "image"] }

The filter should like: [{\"id\":\"script_status\", \"logic\":{}, \"value\":[\"allowed\"]}], then URL encode this filter string and put this in filter parameter.

The available \"id\" of filter are [\"script_status\", \"script_risk\", \"script_review_status\", \"script_id\", \"app_id\"].

Example: { \"id\": \"script_status\", \"logic\": { \"is\": { \"string\": true } }, \"value\": [\"allowed\"] }

Example: { \"id\": \"script_risk\", \"logic\": { \"is\": { \"string\": true } }, \"value\": [\"High\", \"Medium\"] }

Example: { \"id\": \"script_review_status\", \"logic\": { \"is\": { \"string\": true } }, \"value\": [\"needs review\"] }

Valid script_risk values: [\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\", \"Very High\", \"No Data\"].

Valid script_status values: [\"allowed\", \"blocked\"].

Valid script_review_status values: [\"reviewed\", \"needs review\"]

Filter conditions for header events. This parameter uses the same JSON format as the UI filter component.

Raw JSON format (before URL encoding):
[
  {
    "id": "reviewed",            // field name: reviewed / risk / header_name / changed_ts
    "logic": {
      "is": {"string": "true"},
      "search": "string"
    },
    "value": ["false"]          // array of values for this field
  },
  {
    "id": "risk",
    "logic": {
      "is": {"string": "true"},
      "search": "string"
    },
    "value": ["High"]
  }
]

The JSON string must be URL-encoded when sent as a query parameter.

Available field ids: `risk` (Very Low, Low, Medium, High, Very High), `reviewed` (true, false), `header_name`, `changed_ts` (range).
Example (raw JSON): [{"id":"reviewed","logic":{"is":{"string":"true"},"search":"string"},"value":["false"]},{"id":"risk","logic":{"is":{"string":"true"},"search":"string"},"value":["High"]}]

Array like string. Each element shall be JSON like object. 
Basic structure is
```
[
    {
        "id":"{log_field_name}",
        "logic":{
            "is":{"string":true},
            "NOT":{1 or None},
            "RANGE":{1 or None}
        },
        "value":["{field_value_1}", "field_value_2"]
    }
]
```
Add NOT:1 to exclude given values. Add RANGE:1 to tell that the given filter value is range type (at least two values).
Value is an array containing multiple values. The logic between these values is OR logic.

get.description:
Return built-in rule templates to help create rules quickly. Templates include `template_id`, `name`, `description`, and `conditions` only.

Condition object schema:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["field", "operator", "value"],
  "properties": {
    "field": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["level", "body", "service", "username", "action", "module"],
      "description": "Filter field mapped to backend log attributes (note: 'message' maps to 'body' at sender)."
    },
    "operator": {"type": "string", "enum": ["is", "is_not"], "description": "Match operator"},
    "value": {"type": "string", "maxLength": 100, "description": "Non-empty match value"}
  }
}
```

